---
import Explorer from "../components/Explorer";
import "../styles/global.css";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Corpus graph - public-record entity index</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Public-document corpus turned into a queryable entity graph in Postgres. People, organisations, registry identifiers, dated edges, traversal, shortest path, and byte-exact provenance."
    />
    <!-- favicons (generated by build_favicon_set) -->
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="any" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="16x16" href="/favicon-16.png" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="32x32" href="/favicon-32.png" />
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" sizes="180x180" href="/apple-touch-icon.png" />
    <link rel="manifest" href="/site.webmanifest" />
  </head>
  <body class="mx-auto max-w-[1600px] p-3">
    <header class="mb-3 border-b-2 border-[var(--color-ink)] pb-2">
      <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4">
        <h1 class="text-[15px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.08em]">
          Corpus graph &mdash; public-record entity index
        </h1>
        <span class="text-[11px] text-[var(--color-ink-muted)]">
          POSTGRES 17.6 &middot; PGROUTING 3.4.1 &middot; POSTGREST
        </span>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-1 max-w-[110ch] text-[12px] text-[var(--color-ink-muted)]">
        An Australian council's minutes, committee papers, contracts registers
        and tender notices (2015-2026), plus seven US federal references,
        extracted to text and indexed as a graph database in ordinary Postgres.
        The counts above are live from the database, and they are the corpus.
        Entities are people, organisations, checksum-validated ABNs, and
        citations. Edges are co-occurrence within a 400-character window, dated
        by their document, so every query has an as-at form. Traversal is a
        recursive CTE, shortest path and components are pgrouting, and the
        whole read surface is PostgREST over one edge table.
      </p>
    </header>

    <!--
      client:load, not client:visible. The explorer IS the page - deferring
      hydration until scroll would leave an empty shell above the fold.
    -->
    <Explorer client:load />

    <footer
      class="mt-4 border-t border-[var(--color-hairline-strong)] pt-2 text-[11px] text-[var(--color-ink-muted)]"
    >
      <p>
        Extraction is deterministic where the source is regular: citations and
        registry identifiers are grammatically fixed, so those entities and
        edges are verifiable against the source text with no model in the loop.
        Person and organisation extraction is candidate generation - names are
        pattern-matched, not model-recognised, and a production pipeline puts
        an LLM pass and a human review step here.
      </p>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
